     "notes": {
      "text": "2.Nf3 attacks your e5 pawn. 2...Nc6 is the main line: it develops a piece, defends e5 and controls d4. 2...d6 defends with a pawn but falls behind in development, and 2...f6? weakens your king. 2...Nf6 counter-attacks e4 instead.",
