     "notes": {
      "text": "White's bishop eyes f7, your weakest pawn, but there is no immediate threat. 3...Nf6, the Two Knights, develops and attacks e4; it leads to sharp play. 3...Bc5, the Giuoco Piano, keeps the queen's control of g5 and gives a quieter game. If White defends e4 with 4.Nc3, the fork trick 4...Nxe4 5.Nxe4 d5 wins the piece back.",
      "credit": {
       "source": "Wikibooks, Chess Opening Theory/1. e4/1...e5/2. Nf3/2...Nc6/3. Bc4",
